CAT = "zare5Licence"; SEG = "LIC"
Q = [
("Who may carry on business as a financial services provider?",
 "A person licensed under FAIS", ["Anyone registered with CIPC", "Anyone employed by an insurer", "Anyone with a matric certificate"],
 "No person may act or offer to act as an FSP unless issued with a licence by the Authority. Company registration or employment by an insurer does not authorise anyone."),
("An FSP's licence is issued by:",
 "The FSCA", ["The Ombud for FSPs", "The Council for Medical Schemes", "The Financial Intelligence Centre"],
 "The FSCA, as the Authority under the FAIS Act, issues, suspends and withdraws FSP licences."),
("An FSP's licence lists the categories and products it may deal in. Its representative may render services:",
 "Only within that licence", ["In any product they trained in", "In any category for 12 months", "In any product of the same supplier"],
 "Representatives act under the FSP's licence and cannot go beyond the categories and products for which the FSP is authorised."),
("An FSP must show that it is an authorised FSP:",
 "In adverts and business papers", ["Only on its own website", "Only when a client asks", "Only in its annual report"],
 "A licensee must show that it is a licensed FSP in its advertisements, brochures and business documentation, so clients can see its status."),
("Under the FAIS Act, a certified copy of the FSP's licence must be:",
 "Shown at its business premises", ["Sent to each new client", "Lodged with the Ombud for FSPs", "Given to each product supplier"],
 "Section 8(8)(a) of the FAIS Act requires a licensee to display a certified copy of the licence in a prominent and durable manner within every business premises."),
("While an FSP's licence is suspended, its representatives may:",
 "Not render new financial services", ["Keep rendering services as usual", "Move clients to their own licence", "Continue for 90 days"],
 "A suspended FSP and its representatives may not render financial services, apart from what the Authority allows to wind down or complete existing business."),
("Except in urgent cases, before the Authority suspends or withdraws a licence it must:",
 "Give notice and hear the FSP", ["Get a High Court order first", "Obtain the Ombud's approval", "Publish the plan for a year"],
 "The Authority must inform the FSP of its intention and reasons and give it a reasonable opportunity to make submissions, which it then considers."),
("Which is a ground on which the Authority may suspend or withdraw an FSP's licence?",
 "It is no longer fit and proper", ["It has fewer than ten clients", "It sells one supplier's products", "It uses an outside compliance officer"],
 "Failing to meet the fit and proper requirements, or materially breaching the Act, are grounds for suspension or withdrawal. Serving few clients or one supplier is not."),
("Who keeps the official register of authorised FSPs?",
 "The Authority", ["Each product supplier", "The Ombud for FSPs", "The Financial Intelligence Centre"],
 "The Authority keeps a register of licensed FSPs, which the public can search to check a provider's status."),
("A client wants to confirm that an FSP is authorised. The most reliable place to check is:",
 "The FSCA's register of FSPs", ["The FSP's own brochure", "A supplier's list of brokers", "The Ombud's annual report"],
 "The Authority's public register shows whether a provider is licensed and for which categories. An FSP's own material is not independent proof."),
("A broker's accreditation under the Medical Schemes Act lapses. The broker may then:",
 "Not act as a medical scheme broker", ["Carry on under the FAIS licence alone", "Carry on until the renewal date", "Act only for the scheme's trustees"],
 "Medical scheme brokers must be accredited by the Council for Medical Schemes. Without accreditation they may not render broker services to scheme members or be paid compensation for them."),
("To advise on and sell medical scheme options, a broker needs:",
 "FAIS authority and CMS accreditation", ["Only an FAIS licence for the products", "Only CMS accreditation", "Registration with the HPCSA as well"],
 "Health service benefits are FAIS financial products, and the Medical Schemes Act separately requires broker accreditation from the Council for Medical Schemes."),
("Who may declare a business practice undesirable under the FAIS Act?",
 "The Authority", ["The Ombud for FSPs", "Any product supplier", "An FSP's compliance officer"],
 "The Authority may declare a business practice undesirable for all FSPs or a category of them."),
("Before the Authority declares a business practice undesirable, it must normally:",
 "Publish a notice for comment", ["Obtain a High Court order", "Get every FSP's consent", "Wait for three client complaints"],
 "Under section 34(3) of the FAIS Act, the Authority must first publish its intention, with reasons, in the Gazette and invite written representations within 21 days."),
("Once a business practice has been declared undesirable, an FSP must:",
 "Stop carrying on that practice", ["Disclose it to clients and continue", "Apply for an exemption first", "Report it to the Ombud yearly"],
 "After the declaration, no FSP may carry on the undesirable practice, directly or indirectly."),
("A business practice is likely to be undesirable if it:",
 "Unreasonably harms clients", ["Earns the FSP a large profit", "Uses direct marketing", "Involves one product supplier"],
 "The Authority considers whether a practice harms the relationship between FSPs and clients, unreasonably prejudices or deceives clients, or unfairly affects them."),
("An FSP has carried on a practice after it was declared undesirable. The Authority may direct the FSP to:",
 "Put right what it caused", ["Pay the Ombud's running costs", "Replace its compliance officer", "Re-register all its clients"],
 "Under section 34(5) and (6) of the FAIS Act, the Authority may direct the FSP to rectify anything caused by the practice, and the FSP must do so within 60 days."),
("Falsely claiming to be an authorised FSP is:",
 "An offence under the FAIS Act", ["Only a breach of the Code", "Allowed if nothing is sold", "A matter for the Ombud only"],
 "Holding oneself out as an authorised FSP or representative without authority is an offence under the Act."),
("A person convicted of an offence under the FAIS Act may be sentenced to:",
 "A fine or imprisonment", ["A written warning only", "Debarment only", "A civil damages claim only"],
 "The Act provides for a fine or imprisonment, or both, on conviction. Debarment is an administrative step, not a criminal sentence."),
("To help the FSP keep its licence in good standing, a representative must:",
 "Act within the mandate the FSP gives", ["Hold a personal FSP licence", "Approve the annual financial statements", "Appoint the compliance officer"],
 "A representative renders services only within the mandate and the FSP's licence. Licensing, statements and appointments are the FSP's and key individuals' duties."),
("Under the FAIS Act, an FSP must keep:",
 "Accounting records and audited statements", ["A branch office in each province", "A minimum of five representatives", "A client helpline open all night"],
 "FSPs must maintain full and proper accounting records and have their annual financial statements audited, and submit them as the Authority requires."),
("An FSP's licence has been withdrawn. The FSP must:",
 "Stop its financial services", ["Carry on until clients are told", "Hand its clients to the Ombud", "Ask the Ombud for a new licence"],
 "Without a licence the person may not act as an FSP, and it must make arrangements for its existing clients as the Authority directs."),
("Among the licence requirements, 'operational ability' means the FSP has:",
 "Adequate systems and resources", ["A minimum number of clients", "Offices in two cities", "A five-year investment track record"],
 "Operational ability covers having the governance, infrastructure, systems and staff to render the authorised services properly."),
("An FSP must stay financially sound, which includes:",
 "Paying its debts when due", ["Paying clients a yearly bonus", "Owning its own office premises", "Making a profit every year"],
 "The financial soundness requirements look at whether the FSP can meet its liabilities and keep adequate assets and liquidity."),
]
